## Frequently Asked Questions

### **Does Medicare Advantage cover online or virtual therapy in Texas?**

Yes. Medicare Advantage plans cover telehealth counseling sessions delivered via secure video or phone platforms, provided the service is delivered by an eligible, in-network mental health provider.

### **Do I need a doctor's referral to see a therapist with Medicare Advantage?**

It depends on your plan structure. If you have an HMO plan, you will likely need a referral from your primary care physician before insurance covers your sessions. If you have a PPO plan, a referral is usually not required.

### **What is the difference between an LPC, LMFT, and Psychiatrist under Medicare?**

Licensed Professional Counselors (LPCs) and Licensed Marriage and Family Therapists (LMFTs) provide outpatient talk therapy and behavioral interventions. Psychiatrists are medical doctors who primarily diagnose psychiatric conditions and manage medications. As of 2024, Medicare covers services from all these provider types.

### **What if my preferred therapist is not in my Medicare Advantage network?**

If a therapist is out-of-network, you may still be able to receive care. Depending on your plan (especially PPO plans), you may have out-of-network benefits, or you can choose to pay out-of-pocket using self-pay rates.

### Emergency & Crisis Safety Resources

> **Medical Disclaimer:** This article is for informational purposes only and does not constitute medical advice or a clinical diagnosis.

If you or someone you know is facing a mental health crisis, immediate assistance is available 24/7:

- **National Suicide and Crisis Lifeline:** Call or text **988**

- **The Crisis Text Line:** Text **HOME to 741741**

- **Emergency Services:** Call **911** or go to the nearest hospital emergency room.

